  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security for vulnerable groups affected by the food price increase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In total in Kenya, 18,660 direct participants will benefit from the project: 7,450 men (40%) and 11,150 women (60%)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Goal (Impact): Increase in food security and resilience of vulnerable populations to the negative impacts of food price increases and to contribute to the promotion of gender equity&#x200b;.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project will build on the successes of the recently completed BMZ SEWOH project , with the specific aim of scaling up and expanding the interventions that proved most effective and relevant in the previous project, in order to increase the food security and resilience of households most affected by rising food prices, and promote gender equity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NO-BRC-971277882" role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NORAD</narrative>
  </participating-org>
